All written by moist-mason, hence the use of first person.

CURRENT [0.4.0]
- Logging
	- Ensure that most exceptions call the AcpException class, so that they appear in logs if something arises.
- General
	- Figure out how to fix the dependency resolving messages from showing in logs, even if the dependencies are actually resolved.
		- UPDATE 12/15: Dependency resolution needs to happen, so any condition that prevents the ResolveLibraries or ResolveTools steps will make
		Java processes fail. I will continue to find a workaround but this may actually be a necessary evil.

FUTURE [1.0]
- General
	- Rework of the ModLoader download system. Instead of LZMA I am considering using a DiffPatch system, which is
    what NeoForge uses. This will allow the ModLoader text to be more readable, and will be especially important as future versions of Minecraft,
    which rely on Forge, become supported by ACP. This will make the RepackageDefaults class obsolete.
    - Include Reobfuscation SRGs (in .srg) format in the AcpGen data ZIPs, and remove the MakeReobfSrg step.